# ServiceLoader registration for the always-available fallback enhancer.
#
# Why this file exists at all, given that ImageEnhancer.discover() already ends with
# `.orElseGet(PassthroughEnhancer::new)`:
#
#   * The fallback in discover() is a safety net for the case where the classpath is genuinely empty --
#     which is what pip-core's own test asserts, and why PassthroughEnhancer is NOT registered in
#     pip-core/src/main/resources (see the comment in pip-native's copy of this descriptor).
#   * In an assembled application, "which providers are on the classpath" should be answerable by reading
#     these descriptors rather than by reading discover()'s last line. Registering the fallback here makes
#     the full candidate set visible in one place, and makes a DEBUG-level ServiceLoader trace show the
#     selection actually happening instead of a silent orElseGet.
#
# Priority keeps this harmless: PassthroughEnhancer#priority() returns Integer.MIN_VALUE, so any real
# provider -- NativeImageEnhancer, or a future one -- outranks it whenever it reports isAvailable().
#
# ServiceLoader merges descriptors across the classpath, so this file and pip-native's are both read; it
# does not override anything.
com.parallelimage.core.spi.PassthroughEnhancer
